 "area": "A100",
 "areaName": "Tank farm",
 "type": "SR",
 "typeName": "Spool replacement",
 "priority": 2,
 "issuedBy": "Facility owner (demonstration)",
 "notice": "DEMONSTRATION ONLY — NOT A QUALIFIED PROCEDURE; THE FACILITY OWNER'S QUALIFIED PROCEDURES AND APPLICABLE CODES GOVERN.",
 "reason": "External corrosion found on the tank outlet line at the first bend.",
 "scope": [
  "Isolate per the isolation list; drain, vent and purge 6\"-P150-P-1001 between the isolations; confirm gas-free for hot work.",
  "Remove spool 6\"-P150-P-1001-SP02 (7 items, 37'-0\" of pipe) — cut at the field welds and break the flanged joints at its ends as listed.",
  "Fabricate the replacement spool to ISO-6\"-P150-P-1001 with the same items (parts list), welding to WS-01; 6 shop welds.",
  "Install the spool; make 2 field welds; new gaskets and studs at flanged ends, tightened per SW-WO-5.",
  "NDE per the NDE table; hydrostatic test at 210 psi for 30 minutes with the relief valves blinded (SW-TEST-1).",
  "Remove blinds, restore the line-up, hand back."
 ],
